<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="Nfty.App.Views.BrandMarkView">
  <!--
    THE BRAND MARK: the application icon's own symbol, at tile size.

    The mark used to be a lowercase "n" turned 45 degrees, drawn in the mono face. It is the layer
    stack now, which is what the shipped icon carries (corderro-artz.github.io/public/nfty) - a
    letter rotated into a diamond said the name and nothing about the product, while three offset
    diamonds are what an asset IS here: a stack of layers, the top one live.

    TWO diamonds, not the icon's three. This box is 24px and the shipped favicon makes the same cut
    at 64 for the same reason - at this size a third row is a smear rather than a layer, and the
    stack reads from two. The card with all three is the 256px form.

    One control, used by the titlebar and by the quick-reference sheet, because a mark stated twice
    is a mark that drifts: the sheet's tile had already become a plain rotated square while the
    titlebar's was a letter, and nothing in the product said they were meant to be the same thing.

    Theme-aware by construction rather than by a second drawing: the ink is FgBrush and the live
    layer is AccentBrush, so the light and dark dictionaries supply their own values and there is no
    second mark to keep in step - the same argument the icon set itself runs on.
  -->
  <Border Width="24" Height="24" CornerRadius="{DynamicResource RadiusSm}"
          Background="{DynamicResource AccentWashBrush}"
          BorderBrush="{DynamicResource AccentLineBrush}" BorderThickness="1"
          ClipToBounds="True">
    <!-- Authored at final size in an 18x16 box rather than in the icons' shared 24-unit box and
         scaled: Path.ico's scale transform is the ICON system, one stroked path in one brush, and
         this is two paths in two inks. Sized so the strokes land near whole pixels at the shell's
         1.2 scale. The gap is 2 units against a 1.4 stroke - the 256px card had these overlapping
         at first, which reads as a lattice rather than a stack. -->
    <Canvas Width="18" Height="16" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
      <Path Data="M0,4 L9,1 L18,4 L9,7 Z" Fill="{DynamicResource AccentBrush}" />
      <Path Data="M0,12 L9,9 L18,12 L9,15 Z" Stroke="{DynamicResource FgBrush}"
            StrokeThickness="1.4" StrokeJoin="Miter" Opacity="0.75" />
    </Canvas>
  </Border>
</UserControl>
